{"diagnosis": "256-word NOP (ADDI x0,x0,0, opcode 0010011) fetch traps with `TRAP: cpu trap asserted` and `FAIL 0xdead` instead of advancing. Expected `is_alu_reg_imm` to assert for opcode 0010011, but picorv32.v:877 compares to 7'b1010011 so it never asserts. Root cause is wrong opcode constant for `is_alu_reg_imm`, leaving all OP-IMM/NOP undecodable and causing illegal-instruction trap.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -874,6 +874,6 @@
 			is_beq_bne_blt_bge_bltu_bgeu <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1100011;
 			is_lb_lh_lw_lbu_lhu          <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0000011;
 			is_sb_sh_sw                  <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0100011;
-			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1010011;
+			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010011;
 			is_alu_reg_reg               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0110011;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (FAIL 0xdead cleared) with no TRAP: cpu trap asserted"}

